        "blocks": {
          "what": {
            "type": "richtext",
            "settings": {
              "content": {
                "en": "<h2>What are copper uglies?</h2><p>&ldquo;Copper uglies&rdquo; is slang from forums and videos. People use it for skin that looks worse after starting a copper peptide product, with redness, flaking, dullness or a crinkled, crepey look. Some also describe a hollow look under the eyes.</p><p>It is not a term from dermatology, and it has no agreed definition. That matters, because it means two people using the phrase may be describing quite different things.</p>"
              }
            }
          },
          "trial": {
            "type": "richtext",
            "settings": {
              "content": {
                "en": "<h2>Is it a real side effect? What the one trial recorded</h2><p>The question behind &ldquo;side effects of copper peptides&rdquo; is simple: what happened to real people in a controlled study? The only controlled facial trial of GHK-Cu on its own is Badenhorst 2016, which we appraise in full in <a href=\"/blogs/clinical-studies/copper-peptide-wrinkle-trial-badenhorst-2016\">our article on the Badenhorst 2016 trial</a>.</p><ul><li>40 women aged 40 to 65 used a GHK-Cu serum twice a day for 8 weeks.</li><li>39 of the 40 tolerated it. The authors report none of the peeling, dryness or redness they were watching for.</li><li>One woman had minor skin reactions on both sides of her face. She stopped using the products, and the symptoms settled without medical treatment.</li></ul>"
              }
            }
          },
          "care": {
            "type": "richtext",
            "settings": {
              "content": {
                "en": "<p>Read this with care. The trial was funded by the company that makes the serum. It never stated how much GHK-Cu the serum contained, so the result belongs to that serum, not to ours. Our 2% products have no tolerance study of their own.</p>"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "block_order": ["what", "trial", "care"],
        "custom_css": [
