              "text_color": "#1a1a1a",
              "content": {
                "en": "<h2>Could the rest of your routine be the cause?</h2><p>Quite possibly. A copper peptide is rarely the only new thing. Pure L-ascorbic acid, strong exfoliating acids and high-strength retinol can each irritate skin by themselves, and no combination with a copper peptide has been trialled.</p><p>Use those at a different time of day from your copper peptide, and add only one new product at a time. If you change three things at once, you cannot tell which one your skin is reacting to.</p>"
