              "title": {
                "en": "Do copper peptides help with wrinkles?"
              },
              "content": {
                "en": "<p>In Badenhorst 2016, wrinkle volume near the eye fell 24.1% with a GHK-Cu serum, against 15.0% with the plain serum base, over 8 weeks in 20 women, which the paper reports as a 55.8% greater reduction than the plain serum base. The base lacked the nano-carrier as well as the peptide, so the gap covers both. It is one small, maker-funded trial.</p>"
              }
            }
          },
          "q2": {
            "type": "item",
            "settings": {
              "title": {
                "en": "What are the common side effects of copper peptides?"
              },
              "content": {
                "en": "<p>In the one controlled trial, 1 of 40 women had minor skin reactions that settled after she stopped. Beyond that, no study has set out to list the side effects of copper peptides, so we do not claim a full list.</p>"
              }
            }
          }
        },
